WEBVTT

00:00:00.739 --> 00:00:03.541
Previously on Supernatural

00:00:03.576 --> 00:00:04.587
Sammy.

00:00:05.047 --> 00:00:06.930
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can.

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:07.814
Go!

00:00:10.652 --> 00:00:12.869
Dad's on a hunting trip.

00:00:12.904 --> 00:00:15.187
And he hasn't been home in a few days.

00:00:18.266 --> 00:00:19.443
This is dad's book.

00:00:19.478 --> 00:00:21.570
I think dad wants us to
pick up where he left off.

00:00:21.605 --> 00:00:23.619
You know, saving people. Hunting things.

00:00:23.654 --> 00:00:25.209
The family business.

00:00:25.376 --> 00:00:26.680
I got to find dad.

00:00:26.715 --> 00:00:28.974
That's the only thing I can think about.

00:01:57.419 --> 00:01:58.806
I know you're just doing your job

00:01:58.841 --> 00:02:01.162
But the police have
been here a week already.

00:02:01.197 --> 00:02:03.448
I don't see why we have
to go through this again.

00:02:03.483 --> 00:02:06.454
The more he tells the story
the more he believes it's true.

00:02:06.489 --> 00:02:07.917
Mrs. McKay.

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:11.522
We know you spoke with
the local authorities.

00:02:11.657 --> 00:02:15.467
But this seems like a matter
for the State Police. So...

00:02:15.502 --> 00:02:18.141
Don't worry about how
crazy it sounds Evan.

00:02:18.176 --> 00:02:20.274
You just tell us what you saw.

00:02:20.309 --> 00:02:22.445
I was up late...

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.547
Watching TV.

00:02:24.583 --> 00:02:26.340
When I heard this...

00:02:26.375 --> 00:02:28.145
Weird noise.

00:02:28.180 --> 00:02:31.254
What did it sound like?

00:02:31.289 --> 00:02:34.329
It sounded like a monster.

00:02:35.793 --> 00:02:39.013
Tell the officers what
you were watching on TV.

00:02:39.049 --> 00:02:40.728
Um...

00:02:41.272 --> 00:02:44.249
Godzilla versus Mothra.

00:02:44.284 --> 00:02:46.313
That's my favorite Godzilla movie.

00:02:46.348 --> 00:02:48.306
So much better than the original?

00:02:48.342 --> 00:02:49.128
Totally.

00:02:49.163 --> 00:02:51.533
Yeah, he likes the remake.

00:02:51.723 --> 00:02:53.033
Yuck.

00:02:53.068 --> 00:02:54.757
That's what I mean.

00:02:57.168 --> 00:02:58.388
Evan?

00:02:58.815 --> 00:03:01.142
Did you see what this thing was?

00:03:01.177 --> 00:03:03.523
No, but I saw it grab Mr. Jenkins.

00:03:03.558 --> 00:03:05.869
It pulled him underneath the car.

00:03:06.271 --> 00:03:07.485
Then what?

00:03:09.418 --> 00:03:11.647
It took him away.

00:03:11.682 --> 00:03:14.924
I heard the monster leaving.

00:03:14.959 --> 00:03:17.838
It made this really scary sound.

00:03:18.794 --> 00:03:20.718
What did it sound like, Evan?

00:03:21.277 --> 00:03:25.444
Like this whining growl.

00:03:28.358 --> 00:03:29.795
Thanks for your time.

00:03:34.299 --> 00:03:36.697
So the local police
have novel out foul play.

00:03:37.334 --> 00:03:39.171
Apparently there were signs of struggle.

00:03:39.948 --> 00:03:41.842
You know, they could be right.
Could just be a kidnapping.

00:03:42.579 --> 00:03:44.635
Maybe this isn't our kind of gig.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:46.159
Yeah, maybe not.

00:03:46.194 --> 00:03:47.612
Except for this.

00:03:47.647 --> 00:03:49.829
Dad marked the area, Dean.

00:03:49.864 --> 00:03:52.541
Possible hunting grounds
of a phantom attacker.

00:03:52.576 --> 00:03:54.389
Why would he even do that?

00:03:54.424 --> 00:03:58.690
Well, he found a lot of local folk law
about a dog figure that comes out at night,

00:03:58.725 --> 00:04:01.326
Grabs people then vanishes.

00:04:01.361 --> 00:04:02.963
He found this too.

00:04:02.999 --> 00:04:08.144
This county has more missing persons per
capital than anywhere else in the state.

00:04:08.563 --> 00:04:09.540
It is weird.

00:04:10.026 --> 00:04:10.916
Yeah.

00:04:10.989 --> 00:04:13.965
Don't phantom attackers usually
snatch people from their beds?

00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:15.523
Jenkins was taken from a parking lot.

00:04:15.558 --> 00:04:17.046
Well, there are all kinds, you know.

00:04:17.047 --> 00:04:21.404
Spring Hill Jack, Spanworm Gases,
they take people anywhere, anytime.

00:04:21.439 --> 00:04:23.579
Look, Dean. I don't know if
this is our kind of gig either...

00:04:23.614 --> 00:04:26.674
Yeah, you're right. We should
ask around more tomorrow.

00:04:26.709 --> 00:04:28.139
Right.

00:04:29.185 --> 00:04:31.569
I saw a motel about five miles back.

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:33.123
Whoa, whoa, easy.

00:04:33.158 --> 00:04:35.083
Let's have another round?

00:04:35.249 --> 00:04:36.678
We should get an early start.

00:04:36.713 --> 00:04:39.893
Now, you really know how to
have fun, don't you Grandma?

00:04:41.816 --> 00:04:42.934
You're right.

00:04:44.025 --> 00:04:46.012
I'll meet you outside.
I'm gonna take a leak.

00:06:34.104 --> 00:06:35.491
Hey, hey.

00:06:35.526 --> 00:06:38.413
Have you guys been outside? Around
here like the last hour or so?

00:06:39.834 --> 00:06:41.006
Sam?

00:06:43.725 --> 00:06:45.089
Sammy!

00:07:04.473 --> 00:07:06.062
Sam...

00:07:17.774 --> 00:07:20.828
So, what can we do for
you Officer Washington?

00:07:20.863 --> 00:07:22.759
I'm working a missing persons.

00:07:22.794 --> 00:07:25.931
I didn't know the Jenkins case was
being covered by the State Police?

00:07:25.966 --> 00:07:28.357
Uh, no, no. It's someone else.

00:07:28.392 --> 00:07:30.079
Actually it's my cousin.

00:07:30.114 --> 00:07:33.251
We were having a few laughs at
this bar down by the highway.

00:07:33.287 --> 00:07:35.140
And I haven't seen him since.

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:38.128
Did your cousin have a drinking problem?

00:07:38.163 --> 00:07:40.736
Sam? Two beers and he's doing Karaoke.

00:07:40.979 --> 00:07:43.917
No, he wasn't drunk. He was taken.

00:07:45.884 --> 00:07:47.808
All right. What's his name?

00:07:47.843 --> 00:07:49.314
Winchester.

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:52.074
Sam Winchester.

00:07:52.618 --> 00:07:53.807
Like the riffle?

00:07:54.034 --> 00:07:55.505
Like the riffle.

00:07:55.630 --> 00:07:57.226
Winchester, Sam

00:08:02.155 --> 00:08:04.128
Samuel Winchester.

00:08:04.163 --> 00:08:09.811
So you know that his brother
Dean Winchester died in St. Louis.

00:08:09.978 --> 00:08:12.822
And it was excepted a murder.

00:08:13.421 --> 00:08:15.081
Yeah, Dean.

00:08:15.685 --> 00:08:17.884
Kind of the black sheep of the family.

00:08:17.919 --> 00:08:19.420
Handsome though.

00:08:24.461 --> 00:08:26.249
Well, he's not showing up
at any current field reports.

00:08:26.285 --> 00:08:28.369
I already have a lead.

00:08:29.032 --> 00:08:31.269
I saw surveillance
camera above the highway.

00:08:31.304 --> 00:08:32.808
County traffic cam.

00:08:32.844 --> 00:08:34.004
Right, yeah.

00:08:34.039 --> 00:08:35.662
I'm thinking the camera
picked up whatever took him.

00:08:35.697 --> 00:08:37.711
Oh, whoever.

00:08:39.476 --> 00:08:41.141
Well, I have access to
the traffic cam footage

00:08:41.176 --> 00:08:43.982
Down at the county
works department, but...

00:08:44.017 --> 00:08:46.788
Well... Let me tell
you this the right way.

00:08:46.823 --> 00:08:50.721
Won't you fill out...

00:08:51.459 --> 00:08:53.279
A missing persons report.

00:08:56.397 --> 00:08:58.249
And sit tight over here.

00:08:59.108 --> 00:09:00.550
Officer, look uh...

00:09:01.743 --> 00:09:02.830
He's family.

00:09:03.472 --> 00:09:04.489
And I kind of...

00:09:05.455 --> 00:09:06.455
Look out for the kid.

00:09:07.401 --> 00:09:08.770
You got to let me go with you.

00:09:09.276 --> 00:09:10.748
I'm sorry, I can't do that.

00:09:12.563 --> 00:09:14.075
Well, tell me something.

00:09:14.110 --> 00:09:16.997
Your county has a fair
share of missing persons.

00:09:17.032 --> 00:09:19.841
Any of them come back?

00:09:20.552 --> 00:09:24.192
Sam's my responsibility.
And he's coming back.

00:09:24.227 --> 00:09:26.534
I'm bringing him back.

00:10:13.074 --> 00:10:14.210
Greg.

00:10:14.245 --> 00:10:16.086
I think we've got something.

00:10:17.298 --> 00:10:19.516
These traffic cam take an
image every three seconds.

00:10:19.551 --> 00:10:21.822
It's part of the amber alert program.

00:10:21.857 --> 00:10:26.459
These images were all taken around
the time your cousin Sam disappeared.

00:10:27.212 --> 00:10:28.647
This really isn't what I'm looking for.

00:10:28.682 --> 00:10:29.377
Just wait, wait.

00:10:29.422 --> 00:10:30.607
Next one.

00:10:30.642 --> 00:10:33.779
This one was taken right
after Sam left the bar.

00:10:33.814 --> 00:10:36.582
Look at the back in at that thing.

00:10:37.251 --> 00:10:39.802
Now, look at the plates.

00:10:42.062 --> 00:10:44.035
The plates look new. Probably stolen.

00:10:44.070 --> 00:10:48.336
So, whoever's driving that
rust bucket must be involved.

00:10:55.113 --> 00:10:56.316
Do you hear that engine?

00:10:56.352 --> 00:10:57.586
Yeah.

00:10:58.543 --> 00:11:01.470
Kind of a whining growl, isn't it?

00:11:01.889 --> 00:11:03.813
Sure.

00:11:06.197 --> 00:11:08.164
I'll be damned.

00:11:23.138 --> 00:11:25.021
You're alive?

00:11:25.857 --> 00:11:27.161
Hey, you okay?

00:11:27.196 --> 00:11:30.166
Does it look like I'm doing okay?

00:11:31.297 --> 00:11:32.403
Where are we?

00:11:32.438 --> 00:11:33.973
I don't know.

00:11:34.658 --> 00:11:35.861
Country, I think.

00:11:36.517 --> 00:11:38.093
Smells like the country.

00:11:38.769 --> 00:11:40.289
You're Jenkins, aren't you?

00:11:40.827 --> 00:11:41.752
Yeah.

00:11:43.616 --> 00:11:45.057
Wow, I was looking for you.

00:11:45.389 --> 00:11:46.188
Oh, yeah?

00:11:46.223 --> 00:11:46.988
Yeah.

00:11:47.023 --> 00:11:50.627
Well, no offense. But
this is a piss poor rescue.

00:11:50.662 --> 00:11:54.218
Well, my brother's out there right
now too. He's looking for us. So...

00:11:54.253 --> 00:11:56.369
So, he's not gonna find us.

00:11:56.404 --> 00:11:58.450
We're in the middle of nowhere.

00:11:58.485 --> 00:12:01.413
Waiting for them to come back
and do God knows what to us.

00:12:01.448 --> 00:12:03.177
What are they?

00:12:03.901 --> 00:12:04.617
Have you seen them?

00:12:05.320 --> 00:12:05.547
What are you talking about?

00:12:05.548 --> 00:12:07.436
Whatever grabbed us,
what did they look like?

00:12:07.471 --> 00:12:09.193
See for yourself.

00:12:28.393 --> 00:12:29.529
Leave me alone.

00:12:30.301 --> 00:12:32.200
Don't touch me. Leave me alone!

00:12:49.592 --> 00:12:51.767
I'll be damned.

00:12:54.611 --> 00:12:56.208
They're just people.

00:12:56.243 --> 00:12:59.505
Yeah, what did you expect?

00:12:59.924 --> 00:13:01.575
How often do they feed you?

00:13:01.611 --> 00:13:02.702
Once a day.

00:13:03.020 --> 00:13:06.533
They use that thing over
there to open the cage.

00:13:07.244 --> 00:13:09.084
And that's the only time you see them?

00:13:09.119 --> 00:13:11.510
So far. But I'm waiting.

00:13:11.545 --> 00:13:13.452
Waiting for what?

00:13:13.487 --> 00:13:15.323
Their baiting time, man.

00:13:15.358 --> 00:13:17.590
I think that's the least
of your worries right now.

00:13:17.625 --> 00:13:18.359
Oh, yeah?

00:13:18.394 --> 00:13:18.795
Yeah.

00:13:18.831 --> 00:13:20.089
What do you they want then?

00:13:20.748 --> 00:13:22.644
Depends on who they are.

00:13:22.679 --> 00:13:25.690
They're bunch of psycho
hill-Billy red neck if you ask me.

00:13:25.726 --> 00:13:28.452
Looking for love in
all the wrong places.

00:13:42.879 --> 00:13:45.107
Okay, the next traffic cam

00:13:45.142 --> 00:13:48.739
Is fifty miles from here and your
pickup didn't pass that one. So...

00:13:48.775 --> 00:13:50.722
So, it must have pulled up somewhere.

00:13:51.168 --> 00:13:52.636
I don't see any other roads here.

00:13:53.068 --> 00:13:57.189
Well, a lot of these back woods
properties have their own private roads.

00:13:57.693 --> 00:13:59.029
Great.

00:14:11.935 --> 00:14:13.293
So, Gregory.

00:14:13.810 --> 00:14:14.304
Yeah.

00:14:15.108 --> 00:14:16.353
I ran your badge number.

00:14:16.388 --> 00:14:19.093
It's routine when working
A case with State Police

00:14:19.128 --> 00:14:20.990
For county purposes when we have you.

00:14:21.685 --> 00:14:24.838
And they just got back to me...

00:14:28.473 --> 00:14:30.652
Says here your badge was stolen.

00:14:31.441 --> 00:14:34.655
And there's a picture of you.

00:14:39.372 --> 00:14:40.720
I lost some weight.

00:14:40.756 --> 00:14:43.109
And I got that Michael
Jackson skin disease...

00:14:43.145 --> 00:14:43.890
Okay.

00:14:43.925 --> 00:14:45.409
Would you step out of the car please?

00:14:45.444 --> 00:14:46.315
Look, look, look.

00:14:48.371 --> 00:14:50.546
If you want to arrest me that's fine.

00:14:50.581 --> 00:14:52.763
I'll cooperate. I swear.

00:14:52.799 --> 00:14:54.945
But first please...

00:14:54.980 --> 00:14:55.975
Let me find Sam.

00:14:56.010 --> 00:14:57.536
I don't even know who you are.

00:14:57.859 --> 00:15:00.048
Or if this Sam person is missing.

00:15:00.083 --> 00:15:02.426
Look into my eyes and tell
me if I'm lying about this.

00:15:02.461 --> 00:15:05.930
Identity theft. You're
impersonating an officer.

00:15:06.979 --> 00:15:08.650
Here's the thing. When...

00:15:08.941 --> 00:15:10.799
When we were young...

00:15:10.834 --> 00:15:13.850
I pretty much pulled him from a fire.

00:15:14.891 --> 00:15:18.039
And ever since then I
felt responsible for him.

00:15:18.502 --> 00:15:22.044
You know, like it's my
job to keep him safe.

00:15:24.094 --> 00:15:28.402
I'm just afraid if we
don't find him fast.

00:15:29.364 --> 00:15:31.331
Please...

00:15:31.790 --> 00:15:34.761
He's my family.

00:15:35.555 --> 00:15:37.695
I'm sorry.

00:15:37.730 --> 00:15:40.198
You've given me no choice.

00:15:40.233 --> 00:15:42.666
I have to take you in.

00:15:56.412 --> 00:15:59.362
After we find Sam Winchester.

00:16:02.075 --> 00:16:03.608
What's your name again?

00:16:03.643 --> 00:16:04.922
It's Sam.

00:16:05.488 --> 00:16:08.877
Why won't you give it up
Sammy. There's no way out.

00:16:08.912 --> 00:16:10.507
Don't...

00:16:11.093 --> 00:16:12.641
Call me...

00:16:12.676 --> 00:16:14.188
Sammy.

00:16:16.656 --> 00:16:19.041
What is it?

00:16:23.057 --> 00:16:24.402
It's a bracket.

00:16:24.437 --> 00:16:28.202
Well, thank God a bracket.
Now we got them, huh?

00:16:30.502 --> 00:16:33.096
Must have been a short.

00:16:35.856 --> 00:16:39.161
Maybe you knocked something loose.

00:16:42.047 --> 00:16:43.770
I think you should get
back in there Jenkins.

00:16:43.805 --> 00:16:44.366
What?

00:16:44.843 --> 00:16:46.530
This isn't right.

00:16:46.565 --> 00:16:48.552
Do you want to get out of here?

00:16:48.587 --> 00:16:50.504
Yeah, but that was too easy.

00:16:50.539 --> 00:16:52.756
Look, I'm gonna get out of
here. I'm gonna send help. Okay?

00:16:52.791 --> 00:16:53.616
Okay. Don't worry.

00:16:53.651 --> 00:16:54.313
No.

00:16:54.348 --> 00:16:57.148
I'm serious, Jenkins.
This might be a trap.

00:16:57.183 --> 00:16:59.114
Bye, Sammy.

00:16:59.406 --> 00:17:01.331
Jenkins!

00:17:41.236 --> 00:17:43.202
Thank you.

00:19:16.541 --> 00:19:18.297
Okay, officer.

00:19:18.549 --> 00:19:20.128
Look I'm gonna press my luck.

00:19:20.163 --> 00:19:22.089
Your luck is so pressed.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:24.028
Right.

00:19:24.321 --> 00:19:26.203
I was wondering...

00:19:26.454 --> 00:19:28.859
Why are you helping me out anyway?

00:19:28.894 --> 00:19:31.265
Why don't you just lock me up?

00:19:32.184 --> 00:19:35.531
My brother Riley
disappeared three years ago.

00:19:35.566 --> 00:19:37.922
A lot like Sam.

00:19:37.957 --> 00:19:39.840
We searched for him but...

00:19:39.875 --> 00:19:42.098
Nothing.

00:19:42.768 --> 00:19:45.696
I know what it's like to
feel responsible for someone.

00:19:45.731 --> 00:19:48.038
And for them...

00:19:50.632 --> 00:19:53.209
Come on, let's keep at it.

00:19:56.781 --> 00:19:59.012
Wait, wait. Pull over here. Pull over.

00:20:10.806 --> 00:20:12.979
It's the first turn
off I've seen so far.

00:20:14.056 --> 00:20:15.813
You stay here, I'll check it out.

00:20:15.848 --> 00:20:16.952
No way.

00:20:16.988 --> 00:20:18.057
Hey...

00:20:18.742 --> 00:20:20.561
You're a civilian.

00:20:20.596 --> 00:20:22.345
And a felon, I think.

00:20:22.380 --> 00:20:24.806
I'm not taking you with me.

00:20:25.334 --> 00:20:26.689
You're not going without me.

00:20:29.934 --> 00:20:32.091
All right. You promise...

00:20:32.127 --> 00:20:35.390
You won't get involved.
You let me handle it.

00:20:36.031 --> 00:20:37.373
Yeah, I promise.

00:20:37.408 --> 00:20:39.321
Shake on it.

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:45.136
Oh, come on.

00:20:45.889 --> 00:20:48.196
This is ridiculous.

00:20:48.933 --> 00:20:50.983
Katherine, I really think
you're gonna need my help.

00:20:51.018 --> 00:20:54.371
I'll manage. Thank you.

00:20:57.843 --> 00:21:00.772
I got to start carrying paper clips.

00:21:31.474 --> 00:21:32.884
Hello?

00:21:36.117 --> 00:21:37.971
Anybody home?

00:21:52.975 --> 00:21:54.223
Hi.

00:21:55.568 --> 00:21:57.344
How are you?

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:04.820
Who are you?

00:22:04.855 --> 00:22:09.163
I'm Katherine. I'm a deputy.

00:22:09.199 --> 00:22:11.212
What's your name?

00:22:11.248 --> 00:22:12.851
Missy.

00:22:12.886 --> 00:22:15.353
Missy? That's a pretty name.

00:22:15.389 --> 00:22:17.822
Missy, is your mom home?

00:22:17.857 --> 00:22:20.255
She's dead.

00:22:20.290 --> 00:22:24.138
I'm sorry, what about your dad?

00:22:24.431 --> 00:22:26.732
No?

00:22:27.778 --> 00:22:30.831
Can I come in for a minute?

00:22:31.250 --> 00:22:33.591
I just want you look at a picture.

00:22:33.627 --> 00:22:36.034
Have you seen that guy?

00:22:38.152 --> 00:22:40.515
Look at that picture.

00:22:42.543 --> 00:22:44.056
What?

00:22:44.091 --> 00:22:46.601
That's gonna hurt.

00:22:49.446 --> 00:22:51.083
Missy, sweetheart.

00:22:51.118 --> 00:22:53.629
Go tell your brothers,
I want to see them.

00:22:53.664 --> 00:22:56.222
Yes, daddy.

00:23:12.996 --> 00:23:15.380
Son of a bitch.

00:24:19.202 --> 00:24:21.450
But I've never seen him so angry before.

00:24:21.485 --> 00:24:24.776
Never been followed
by the police before.

00:24:39.866 --> 00:24:42.251
You all right?

00:24:45.304 --> 00:24:48.274
Are you Sam Winchester? Aren't you?

00:24:48.309 --> 00:24:50.069
Yeah.

00:24:50.104 --> 00:24:51.830
You're...

00:24:52.206 --> 00:24:55.553
